From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cy122 <cy122@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: qcom: optionally keep running across system suspend

The qcom watchdog is stopped in the system-suspend callback whenever the
character device is active.  This is safe for normal suspend, but it also
removes the only hardware recovery path when a suspend transition hangs
before the RTC alarm can wake the SoC.

Add a runtime module parameter, disabled by default, which leaves the
watchdog counting through system suspend instead of stopping it.  A test
can arm a bounded watchdog before entering suspend and let a hardware reset
recover the device if resume never completes.

Signed-off-by: cy122 <cy122@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/qcom-wdt.c
@@ -20,6 +20,11 @@ enum wdt_reg {
 
 #define QCOM_WDT_ENABLE		BIT(0)
 
+static bool keep_running_in_suspend;
+module_param(keep_running_in_suspend, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(keep_running_in_suspend,
+		 "Keep the hardware watchdog running across system suspend");
+
 static const u32 reg_offset_data_apcs_tmr[] = {
 	[WDT_RST] = 0x38,
 	[WDT_EN] = 0x40,
@@ -361,8 +366,12 @@ static int __maybe_unused qcom_wdt_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct qcom_wdt *wdt = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	if (watchdog_active(&wdt->wdd))
-		qcom_wdt_stop(&wdt->wdd);
+	if (watchdog_active(&wdt->wdd)) {
+		if (keep_running_in_suspend)
+			qcom_wdt_ping(&wdt->wdd);
+		else
+			qcom_wdt_stop(&wdt->wdd);
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
